-- Row il-67. EXPECTED RED: four assertions that fail on purpose, one per item. Each says that what the citing words reach is in force in the current official text as the instruments read give it, and each is FALSE.
-- I1: every section section 50(a) cites is in force.        False: section 46 is repealed (SH 978 item 2).
-- I2: every section section 51(b)(1) cites is in force.     False: section 46 is repealed.
-- I3: no section the range in section 48 names is repealed. False: the range ends at section 46, which is repealed.
-- I4: the subsection section 57(1) cites is among those of section 52 in force after item 1(2) of SH 1070. False: subsection (c) is not among them.
-- The count, four, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red). If a defect is cured by a later instrument, its assertion turns green and the declared count must go down with it.

